            "review_text": "maryyeo\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam4531 contributions\n0\nTERRIBLE. Their third outlet at Phu My Hung was extremely bad too.\nSep 2020\nWanted to write a review about the outlet at Phu My Hung (PMH) and discovered they have two other outlets in District 1 and 3! Seriously wondered how they were able to open a third outlet at PMH when the reviews of their first two were already so bad.\n\n1) RESERVATION ORDEAL:\nThe entire experience at their third outlet at Phu My Hung was equally atrocious. We made a reservation IN PERSON at 5pm for a table at 7pm. The matre d did not do so when we arrived and looked thoroughly lost at what to do. We waited half an hour just to get in.\n\n2) WAITING ORDEAL:\nUpon entering, it was when I realized why we often see queues outside Chang (which made us curious to try it, in the first place). It honestly WAS NOT because the food was good, it was because they were SERIOUSLY SLOW and EXTREMELY DISORGANIZED. Waited another 20 minutes to get only our first side dish of fried shredded fish. Another 10 minutes later to get a green curry. AND THEN another 10 minutes to get a plate of Kai Lan vegetables that looked like it lost all its leaves. Come on, who orders Kai Lan only for its stems?!? After a grand total of almost an hour, our kids' MAIN DINNER DISH - a simple dish of fried pineapple rice came at almost 8.30pm. \n\n3) LACK OF FOOD ORDEAL:\nCountless customers seemed so glad they finally got a seat after a long wait (because they must have been fooled like us, thinking this place must have great food deserving of a long waiting time)... during our 2-hour ordeal there... and we witnessed so many of them left either because the food was so slow, or because they were told the dishes they ordered WEREN'T AVAILABLE only after they have ordered for a good 10 minutes.\n\n4) NONCHALENT FOOD PREPARERS ORDEAL\nThey also completely MISSED making our dessert (the restaurant was almost half empty by then and the dessert bar food preparer was literally staring at space), and when we received it, it was VERY DIFFERENT from what we ordered because of the large picture of their star dessert that they have featured prominently on their menu - so the differences were simply obvious. \n\nOne of the servers tried hard to help what she could, I could tell. But even she was looking confused as well. It is obvious this restaurant is run by youngsters who weren't given adequate training by management who doesn't care. Hope they can get a job at a better place which will bother to train them better.\n\nNEVER AGAIN are we gonna visit it. And will advise you not to, too.\nRead more\nWritten October 15, 2020",
